# Dependency Inversion Principle (DIP)

- High-level policy code should depend on abstractions, not concrete details.
- Inject infrastructure dependencies (IO, network, DB, framework runtime) behind interfaces/adapters.
- Keep framework-specific code at boundaries.
- Avoid direct construction of concrete dependencies inside core logic when injection is practical.

## Review checklist

- Does core logic import concrete infra classes directly?
- Can this dependency be inverted via protocol/interface + adapter?
- Are side-effecting dependencies isolated at boundaries?
